  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Scattered showers and thunderstorms this afternoon,\nmainly over the North. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nLift from upper level shortwave energy should help to drive \nafternoon shower and thunderstorm development over the North \ntoday. Thinking that most convection will be showers as models \nare showing poor mid-level lapse rates as a result of a mid-\nlevel inversion that may stunt convective growth. The bigger \nquestion is how far south storms will reach which will depend on\nthe location of forcing.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Another round of showers and thunderstorms toward\nthe end of the week. A strong storm or two is possible.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nAn upper level trough digs into ern Canada on Thursday with a \nsurface warm lifting thru the CWA. Showers move in from the west\nin the afternoon with thunderstorms possible during the afternoon\nwith CAPES between 500-1000 J/kg and 0-6km shear > 30kts. This may\nbring strong storms to the area.\n\nWeak low pressure moves thru the area at some point, like Thursday \nnight keeping showers in the area. Upper level trough then progged\nto move thru during the day on Friday, along with the cold pool with\nanother round of storms. \n\nPwats are pretty meager, ranging from 1-1.50 inches, highest over \nDowneast so not seeing the potential for heavy rain at this point. \n\nThe highest tides of the month will be at week/s end but not expecting\nanything impactful at this point.",
